module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.two_declarations_share_one_decl_index_key

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode, RungRead, FoundOnRung, BelowCeiling }
import gunbc.guarantee_rung { Mitigatable, StructurallyImpossible }
import gunbc.rung_climb { ClimbableButUnbuilt }

data two_declarations_share_one_decl_index_key: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "two_declarations_share_one_decl_index_key" as NonEmptyStr,

  rung: RungRead {
    found_at: FoundOnRung { rung: Mitigatable },
    standing: BelowCeiling {
      current: FoundOnRung { rung: Mitigatable },
      ceiling: StructurallyImpossible,
      blocker: ClimbableButUnbuilt,
      trigger_capability: "the seed's decl index key carries the full module path, so two same-named declarations in different modules get distinct keys and a keyed read of one returns only that declaration",
    },
  },

  receipts: [
    "SPECIMEN (NAMESPACE-XL rehoming, wise-moth-707, 2026-10-20, branch wave/rehome): v2.workflow.roster_rehome asked v2.std.decl_index decl_facts_at for v2.std.integer.Int and got no row, then for std.integer.Int and got two. The seed's decl_logical_qualified_name (src/v1/stage0/src/coproduct_reflection.rs) builds a DeclFact's qualified_name from its module path with a leading v2. removed, so v2.std.integer.Int (src/v2/std/integer.dag) and std.integer.Int (dag/std/integer.dag) carry the same key std.integer.Int. The two are different declarations: one is the alias GroupCompletion<Nat>, the other the coproduct NonNegative | Negative.",
    "INVALID STATE: two distinct declarations share one identity key, so a keyed read returns both and the v2-tree name resolves to nothing. This is DESIGN section 3's single-authority break at the identity layer: the qualified name is meant to be the module's own name, and here a second, logical naming stands in for it.",
    "POPULATION MEASURED ON MAIN (2026-10-20, a lexical scan by wise-moth-707 of declarations in module paths present in both the dag and src/v2 trees): 10 module paths exist in both trees and 1 of them, std.integer, shares declaration names. That gives 23 colliding keys, among them Int, Int8, Int16, Int32, Int64 and Int128. The scan is a one-off, not an instrument; the census producer is the decl_index pool itself once the key carries the module name.",
    "EXPOSED CONSUMERS: every reader that keys or joins on DeclFact.qualified_name over a pool covering both trees can return or match the wrong declaration for those 23 keys. By module: v2.std.decl_ref_resolution (decl_facts_at), v2.std.node_reflection (decl_facts_at), v2.std.data_initializer_identity (qualified_name equality), v2.std.decl_facts_skeleton, v2.lens.live_read_classification, gunbc.instruments.v1_consumer_discovery (decl_facts_at), and the witnesses test.claim.documentary_refs_witness, test.claim.serving_caller_backlog_witness, test.claim.decl_fact_value_projection_witness, test.claim.decl_facts_initializer_projection_witness, test.claim.fleet.runtime_identity_match_witness, test.claim.fn_arrow_decl_facts_live_subject_witness, test.claim.content_hash_combine_preimage_witness and v2.test.claim.enforcement_live_witness. Whether a given consumer reaches a colliding key depends on its pool and subject; none is shown wrong here, only exposed.",
    "HARM: a keyed read can silently resolve a v2 declaration to its dag namesake, or report a real ambiguity for an unambiguous name. Rehoming, which matches by declaration identity, cannot name v2.std.integer.Int at all.",
    "RUNG EVIDENCE (wise-moth-707, 2026-10-30): Mitigatable is the rung the interim's design reaches, not one a RED has executed. rehome_sole_fact's typed refusal (rehome-target-file-mismatch) has no discriminating RED among the roster-rehome-controls; the only executed route through the filter is the real Int pair's verdict, a positive control that keeps the one fact on the derived file. Until a control feeds two keyed candidates neither of which is on the derived file and expects the refusal, the refusal arm is unexercised. The ceiling is StructurallyImpossible because once the key is the module's own qualified name, two declarations cannot share one.",
    "INTERIM, DECLARED: v2.workflow.roster_rehome rehome_sole_fact reads the keyed candidates and keeps only the one whose rel_path is the file the one name-to-path rule derives for the home (v2.compiler.source_authority module_file over v2.cli.repository_layout repository_storage_layout); otherwise it refuses typed (rehome-target-file-mismatch, naming the wanted path and the candidates). It reads the storage-layout authority forward and never guesses. DISSOLUTION TRIGGER: the key fix below lands, and rehome_sole_fact goes back to a plain keyed read of <home>.<name>, with BOTH halves deleted: the file filter AND its copy of the seed key rule (stripping a leading v2. from the home), so no second statement of how the key is built outlives the fix.",
    "RUNG FOUND AT: below the ladder for consumers that silently pick the first row; mitigatable where a consumer refuses on multiplicity. CEILING: structurally impossible: the DeclFact key is the declaring module's own qualified name, v2. included, so two declarations can share a key only if they are the same declaration. NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, AS A CAPABILITY: decl_index keys every DeclFact by its module's own name, proved by a control that reads v2.std.integer.Int and std.integer.Int as two single, distinct rows. Routed by tidy-ant-251 into adhoc-0f4309c5-074's scope."
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
